{
  "_doc": [
    "The symbol surface between `ee.schimke.composeai.cli.serve` and the rest of the CLI.",
    "A debt register for the preview-server split (issue #3824), not a config file: entries",
    "only ever come off. `scripts/check-serve-seam.py` fails on a crossing that is not listed",
    "(new coupling) AND on a listed entry that no longer crosses (prune it \u2014 that is progress).",
    "Regenerate the shrunk list with `python3 scripts/check-serve-seam.py --write`.",
    "cliInternalsUsedByServe: serve reaching into the CLI. Each entry is something the extracted",
    "server would have to get from a published contract module instead. The bundle-format cluster",
    "(BundleReader, BundleSigning, BundleClasspathHydration, extractBundle*, locateBundleSidecar*,",
    "BUNDLE_VERSION, ZIP_DOS_EPOCH_MS) is #3824 preparation item 5 and is most of this list.",
    "serveInternalsUsedByCli: the CLI reaching into serve. Each entry must either move to the",
    "server build with serve, or move down into a contract module the CLI can keep using. The",
    "long tail here is ServeCommand.kt, which #3824 wants reduced to a thin entry point.",
    "forbiddenPackages is NOT a ratchet: an extracted preview server never imports a renderer, an",
    "forbiddenPackages is NOT a ratchet: an extracted preview server never imports a renderer, an",
    "MCP server, or the gradle plugin, and there is nothing here to grandfather. `\u2026composeai.plugin`",
    "is the plugin's real namespace (`plugin`, `plugin.daemon`, `plugin.tooling`) \u2014 an earlier",
    "`\u2026composeai.gradle` entry named nothing at all and enforced nothing, while `plugin.tooling`",
    "types sit on the CLI compile classpath via `:gradle-preview-driver`, ready to be reached for.",
    "contractPackages maps each non-`cli` package serve imports to the module that publishes",
    "it, and must agree with `contracts` in preview-server/contract-probe/build.gradle.kts \u2014",
    "that is what stops a hand-maintained coordinate list from silently missing a module serve",
    "has started using. unpublishedContracts records a mapped module that cannot be resolved",
    "as an artifact yet; each one is a split blocker, not an exemption."
  ],
  "forbiddenPackages": [
    "ee.schimke.composeai.renderer",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.mcp",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.plugin"
  ],
  "contractPackages": {
    "ee.schimke.composeai.daemon.protocol": "daemon-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.daemon.devices": "daemon-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.daemon": "daemon-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.designpages": "preview-data-api",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.io": "common-io",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.render.session.subprocess": "render-session-subprocess",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.render.session": "render-session-api",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.data.layoutinspector": "data-layoutinspector-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.data.overrides": "data-preview-overrides-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.data.remotecompose": "data-remotecompose-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.data.theme": "data-theme-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.data.render": "data-render-core",
    "ee.schimke.composeai.daemon.bta": "daemon-bta-host"
  },
  "unpublishedContracts": {
    "daemon-bta-host": "`:daemon:bta-host` has no maven-publishing block, so an extracted server cannot depend on it at all. serve reaches it for the playground's compile path (BtaCompileSession, DiagnosticCollector). Publishing it, or moving the compile session behind a published contract, is a split blocker \u2014 see docs/design/PREVIEW_SERVER_SPLIT.md."
  },
